  "paragraph": 19,
  "text": "Eventually, on a truly long session, even clean context fills up. When usage crosses a high threshold like seventy-five or eighty percent, naive harnesses slice off the oldest messages from the front. That breaks paired tool-call IDs and tool results, and often deletes the user's original goal. Production harnesses run structured compaction instead, distilling completed work, modified files, verified facts, and exact next steps into a fresh checkpoint. You pay a one-time cache reset cleanly, drop usage back near fifteen percent, and keep moving with full clarity.",
